<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theorem Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 Constructing 𝑝_𝑡,𝑢_𝑡 from conditional probability paths and vector fields ‣ 3 Flow Matching ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To verify this, we check that <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the continuity equation (equation <a href="#A2.E26" title="In Appendix B The continuity equation ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\Big(\frac{d}{dt}p_{t}(x|x_{1})\Big)q(x_{1})dx_{1}=-\int\mathrm{div}\Big(u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})\Big)q(x_{1})dx_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\Big(\frac{d}{dt}p_{t}(x|x_{1})\Big)q(x_{1})dx_{1}=-\int\mathrm{div}\Big(u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})\Big)q(x_{1})dx_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathrm{div}\Big(\int u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}\Big)=-\mathrm{div}\Big(u_{t}(x)p_{t}(x)\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathrm{div}\Big(\int u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}\Big)=-\mathrm{div}\Big(u_{t}(x)p_{t}(x)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">where in the second equality we used the fact that <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{t}(\cdot|x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}(\cdot|x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> generates <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{t}(\cdot|x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\cdot|x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, in the last equality we used equation <a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1 Constructing 𝑝_𝑡,𝑢_𝑡 from conditional probability paths and vector fields ‣ 3 Flow Matching ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Furthermore, the first and third equalities are justified by assuming the integrands satisfy the regularity conditions of the Leibniz Rule (for exchanging integration and differentiation).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 Conditional Flow Matching ‣ 3 Flow Matching ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">To ensure existence of all integrals and to allow the changing of integration order (by Fubini’s Theorem) in the following we assume that <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x|x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x|x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> are decreasing to zero at a sufficient speed as <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|x\right\|\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|x\right\|\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t},v_{t},\nabla_{\theta}v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t},v_{t},\nabla_{\theta}v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, using the standard bilinearity of the <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-norm we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|v_{t}(x)-u_{t}(x)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|v_{t}(x)-u_{t}(x)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|v_{t}(x)\right\|^{2}-2\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x)\right\rangle+\left\|u_{t}(x)\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|v_{t}(x)\right\|^{2}-2\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x)\right\rangle+\left\|u_{t}(x)\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|v_{t}(x)-u_{t}(x|x_{1})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|v_{t}(x)-u_{t}(x|x_{1})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|v_{t}(x)\right\|^{2}-2\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\rangle+\left\|u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|v_{t}(x)\right\|^{2}-2\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\rangle+\left\|u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Next, remember that <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and note that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}(x)}\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}(x)}\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2}p_{t}(x)dx=\int\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2}p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2}p_{t}(x)dx=\int\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2}p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{1}),p_{t}(x|x_{1})}\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{1}),p_{t}(x|x_{1})}\|v_{t}(x)\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">where in the second equality we use equation <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.1 Constructing 𝑝_𝑡,𝑢_𝑡 from conditional probability paths and vector fields ‣ 3 Flow Matching ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, and in the third equality we change the order of integration.
Next,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}(x)}\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x)\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p_{t}(x)}\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x)\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\left\langle v_{t}(x),\frac{\int u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}}{p_{t}(x)}\right\rangle p_{t}(x)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\left\langle v_{t}(x),\frac{\int u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}}{p_{t}(x)}\right\rangle p_{t}(x)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\left\langle v_{t}(x),\int u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}\right\rangle dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\left\langle v_{t}(x),\int u_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}\right\rangle dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\rangle p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\rangle p_{t}(x|x_{1})q(x_{1})dx_{1}dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{1}),p_{t}(x|x_{1})}\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{1}),p_{t}(x|x_{1})}\left\langle v_{t}(x),u_{t}(x|x_{1})\right\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">where in the last equality we change again the order of integration.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4 Conditional Probability Paths and Vector Fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For notational simplicity let <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(x)=u_{t}(x|x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(x)=u_{t}(x|x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Now consider equation <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Preliminaries: Continuous Normalizing Flows ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}\psi_{t}(x)=w_{t}(\psi_{t}(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}\psi_{t}(x)=w_{t}(\psi_{t}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible (as <math id="A1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}(x_{1})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}(x_{1})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) we let <math id="A1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\psi^{-1}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\psi^{-1}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and get</span></p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}_{t}(\psi^{-1}(y))=w_{t}(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}_{t}(\psi^{-1}(y))=w_{t}(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the apostrophe notation for the derivative to emphasis that <math id="A1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is evaluated at <math id="A1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{-1}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{-1}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, inverting <math id="A1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> provides</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}^{-1}(y)=\frac{y-\mu_{t}(x_{1})}{\sigma_{t}(x_{1})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}^{-1}(y)=\frac{y-\mu_{t}(x_{1})}{\sigma_{t}(x_{1})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating <math id="A1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}^{\prime}(x)=\sigma_{t}^{\prime}(x_{1})x+\mu_{t}^{\prime}(x_{1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}^{\prime}(x)=\sigma_{t}^{\prime}(x_{1})x+\mu_{t}^{\prime}(x_{1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging these last two equations in equation <a href="#A1.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Theorem Proofs ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> we get</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(y)=\frac{\sigma^{\prime}_{t}(x_{1})}{\sigma_{t}(x_{1})}\left(y-\mu_{t}(x_{1})\right)+\mu_{t}^{\prime}(x_{1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(y)=\frac{\sigma^{\prime}_{t}(x_{1})}{\sigma_{t}(x_{1})}\left(y-\mu_{t}(x_{1})\right)+\mu_{t}^{\prime}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">as required.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>The continuity equation</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One method of testing if a vector field <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> generates a probability path <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the continuity equation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Villani, 2009</a>)</cite>. It is a Partial Differential Equation (PDE) providing a necessary and sufficient condition to ensuring that a vector field <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> generates <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}p_{t}(x)+\mathrm{div}(p_{t}(x)v_{t}(x))=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}p_{t}(x)+\mathrm{div}(p_{t}(x)v_{t}(x))=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the divergence operator, <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{div}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>div</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{div}</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined with respect to the spatial variable <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x^{1},\ldots,x^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x^{1},\ldots,x^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{div}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{div}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{\partial}{\partial x^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Computing probabilities of the CNF model</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We are given an arbitrary data point <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and need to compute the model probability at that point, <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Below we recap how this can be done covering the basic relevant ODEs, the scaling of the divergence computation, taking into account data transformations (<span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, centering of data), and Bits-Per-Dimension computation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ODE for computing <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The continuity equation with equation <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Preliminaries: Continuous Normalizing Flows ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lead to the instantaneous change of variable <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ben-Hamu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\log p_{t}(\phi_{t}(x))+\mathrm{div}(v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x))=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\log p_{t}(\phi_{t}(x))+\mathrm{div}(v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x))=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Integrating <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{1}(\phi_{1}(x))-\log p_{0}(\phi_{0}(x))=-\int_{0}^{1}\mathrm{div}(v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x)))dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{1}(\phi_{1}(x))-\log p_{0}(\phi_{0}(x))=-\int_{0}^{1}\mathrm{div}(v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x)))dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the log probability can be computed together with the flow trajectory by solving the ODE:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{t}(x)\\
f(t)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x))\\
-\mathrm{div}(v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x)))\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{t}(x)\\
f(t)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x))\\
-\mathrm{div}(v_{t}(\phi_{t}(x)))\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Given initial conditions</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{0}(x)\\
f(0)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}x_{0}\\
c\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{0}(x)\\
f(0)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}x_{0}\\
c\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">the solution <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\phi_{t}(x),f(t)\right]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\phi_{t}(x),f(t)\right]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely defined (up to some mild conditions on the VF <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>). Denote <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=\phi_{1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=\phi_{1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and according to equation <a href="#A3.E27" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=c+\log p_{1}(x_{1})-\log p_{0}(x_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=c+\log p_{1}(x_{1})-\log p_{0}(x_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we are given an arbitrary <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and want to compute <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. For this end, we will need to solve equation <a href="#A3.E28" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> in reverse. That is,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{ds}\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{1-s}(x)\\
f(1-s)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}-v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))\\
\mathrm{div}(v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x)))\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{ds}\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{1-s}(x)\\
f(1-s)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}-v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))\\
\mathrm{div}(v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x)))\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and we solve this equation for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with the initial conditions at <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{1}(x)\\
f(1)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}x_{1}\\
0\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{1}(x)\\
f(1)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}x_{1}\\
0\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">From uniqueness of ODEs, the solution will be identical to the solution of equation <a href="#A3.E28" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> with initial conditions in equation <a href="#A3.E29" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a> where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\log p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\log p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be seen from equation <a href="#A3.E30" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a> and setting <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore we get that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\log p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\log p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and consequently</p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x_{1})=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-f(0)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x_{1})=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-f(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">To summarize, to compute <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> we first solve the ODE in equation <a href="#A3.E31" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> with initial conditions in equation <a href="#A3.E32" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, and the compute equation <a href="#A3.E33" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Unbiased estimator to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Solving equation <a href="#A3.E31" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> requires computation of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{div}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>div</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{div}</annotation></semantics></math> of VFs in <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> which is costly. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grathwohl et al. (2018)</a></cite> suggest to replace the divergence by the (unbiased) Hutchinson trace estimator,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{ds}\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{1-s}(x)\\
\tilde{f}(1-s)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}-v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))\\
z^{T}Dv_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))z\end{bmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{ds}\begin{bmatrix}\phi_{1-s}(x)\\
\tilde{f}(1-s)\end{bmatrix}=\begin{bmatrix}-v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))\\
z^{T}Dv_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))z\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sample from a random variable such that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}zz^{T}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}zz^{T}=I</annotation></semantics></math>. Solving the ODE in equation <a href="#A3.E34" title="In Unbiased estimator to 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> exactly (in practice, with a small controlled error) with initial conditions in equation <a href="#A3.E32" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a> leads to</p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\tilde{f}(0)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\tilde{f}(0)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[\tilde{f}(0)-\tilde{f}(1)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[\tilde{f}(0)-\tilde{f}(1)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[\int_{0}^{1}z^{T}Dv_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))z\,ds\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[\int_{0}^{1}z^{T}Dv_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))z\,ds\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[z^{T}Dv_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))z\right]ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}_{z}\left[z^{T}Dv_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x))z\right]ds</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\int_{0}^{1}\mathrm{div}(v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x)))ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\int_{0}^{1}\mathrm{div}(v_{1-s}(\phi_{1-s}(x)))ds</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\left(f(0)-f(1)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\left(f(0)-f(1)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\left(\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\log p_{1}(x_{1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\left(\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\log p_{1}(x_{1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{1}(x_{1})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{1}(x_{1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where in the third equality we switched order of integration assuming the sufficient condition of Fubini’s theorem hold, and in the previous to last equality we used equation <a href="#A3.E30" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>.
Therefore the random variable</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\tilde{f}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{0}(x_{0})-\tilde{f}(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">is an unbiased estimator for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. To summarize, for a scalable unbiased estimation of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> we first solve the ODE in equation <a href="#A3.E34" title="In Unbiased estimator to 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> with initial conditions in equation <a href="#A3.E32" title="In ODE for computing 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, and then output equation <a href="#A3.E35" title="In Unbiased estimator to 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Transformed data</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Often, before training our generative model we transform the data, <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.</span>, we scale and/or translate the data. Such a transformation is denoted by <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{-1}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{-1}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and our generative model becomes a composition</p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi(x)=\varphi\circ\phi(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi(x)=\varphi\circ\phi(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the model we train. Given a prior probability <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> we have that the push forward of this probability under <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> (equation <a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Preliminaries: Continuous Normalizing Flows ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and equation <a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2 Preliminaries: Continuous Normalizing Flows ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) takes the form</p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{1}(x)=\psi_{*}p_{0}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{1}(x)=\psi_{*}p_{0}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{0}(\phi^{-1}(\varphi^{-1}(x)))\det\left[D\phi^{-1}(\varphi^{-1}(x))\right]\det\left[D\varphi^{-1}(x)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{0}(\phi^{-1}(\varphi^{-1}(x)))\det\left[D\phi^{-1}(\varphi^{-1}(x))\right]\det\left[D\varphi^{-1}(x)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))\right)\det\left[D\varphi^{-1}(x)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))\right)\det\left[D\varphi^{-1}(x)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x)=\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))+\log\det\left[D\varphi^{-1}(x)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x)=\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))+\log\det\left[D\varphi^{-1}(x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">For images <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=H\times W\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=H\times W\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> and we consider a transform <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> that maps each pixel value from <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,256]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0,256</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,256]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(y)=2^{7}(y+1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(y)=2^{7}(y+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{-1}(x)=2^{-7}x-1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{-1}(x)=2^{-7}x-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">For this case we have</p>
<table id="A3.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{1}(x)=\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))-7d\log 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{1}(x)=\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))-7d\log 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bits-Per-Dimension (BPD) computation</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">BPD is defined by</p>
<table id="A3.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{BPD}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}}\left[-\frac{\log_{2}p_{1}(x_{1})}{d}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}}\left[-\frac{\log p_{1}(x_{1})}{d\log 2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>BPD</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{BPD}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}}\left[-\frac{\log_{2}p_{1}(x_{1})}{d}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}}\left[-\frac{\log p_{1}(x_{1})}{d\log 2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Following equation <a href="#A3.E36" title="In Transformed data ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a> we get</p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{BPD}=-\frac{\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))}{d\log 2}+7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>BPD</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{BPD}=-\frac{\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))}{d\log 2}+7</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\phi_{*}p_{0}(\varphi^{-1}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> is approximated using the unbiased estimator in equation <a href="#A3.E35" title="In Unbiased estimator to 𝑝_1⁢(𝑥_1) ‣ Appendix C Computing probabilities of the CNF model ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a> over the transformed data <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{-1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{-1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Averaging the unbiased estimator on a large test test <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> provides a good approximation to the test set BPD.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Diffusion conditional vector fields</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the vector field governing the Probability Flow ODE (equation 13 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. (2020b)</a></cite>) for the VE and VP diffusion paths (equation <a href="#S4.E18" title="In Example I: Diffusion conditional VFs. ‣ 4.1 Special instances of Gaussian conditional probability paths ‣ 4 Conditional Probability Paths and Vector Fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) and note that it coincides with the conditional vector fields we derive using Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4 Conditional Probability Paths and Vector Fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, namely the vector fields defined in equations <a href="#S4.E16" title="In Example I: Diffusion conditional VFs. ‣ 4.1 Special instances of Gaussian conditional probability paths ‣ 4 Conditional Probability Paths and Vector Fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> and <a href="#S4.E19" title="In Example I: Diffusion conditional VFs. ‣ 4.1 Special instances of Gaussian conditional probability paths ‣ 4 Conditional Probability Paths and Vector Fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We start with a short primer on how to find a conditional vector field for the probability path described by the Fokker-Planck equation, then instantiate it for the VE and VP probability paths.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since in the diffusion literature the diffusion process runs from data at time <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to noise at time <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we will need the following lemma to translate the diffusion VFs to our convention of <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to noise and <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to data:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a flow defined by a vector field <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> generating probability density path <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the vector field <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{t}(x)=-u_{1-t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{t}(x)=-u_{1-t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> generates the path <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{t}(x)=p_{1-t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{t}(x)=p_{1-t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> when initiated from <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{0}(x)=p_{1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{0}(x)=p_{1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use the continuity equation (equation <a href="#A2.E26" title="In Appendix B The continuity equation ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\tilde{p}_{t}(x)=\frac{d}{dt}p_{1-t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\tilde{p}_{t}(x)=\frac{d}{dt}p_{1-t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-p^{\prime}_{1-t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-p^{\prime}_{1-t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{div}(p_{1-t}(x)u_{1-t}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{div}(p_{1-t}(x)u_{1-t}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathrm{div}(\tilde{p}_{t}(x)(-u_{1-t}(x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathrm{div}(\tilde{p}_{t}(x)(-u_{1-t}(x)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{t}(x)=-u_{1-t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{t}(x)=-u_{1-t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> generates <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conditional VFs for Fokker-Planck probability paths</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a Stochastic Differential Equation (SDE) of the standard form</p>
<table id="A4.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dy=f_{t}dt+g_{t}dw" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dy=f_{t}dt+g_{t}dw</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with time parameter <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, drift <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, diffusion coefficient <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dw" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dw</annotation></semantics></math> is the Wiener process. The solution <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to the SDE is a stochastic process, <span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, a continuous time-dependent random variable, the probability density of which, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(y_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(y_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, is characterized by the Fokker-Planck equation:</p>
<table id="A4.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dp_{t}}{dt}=-\mathrm{div}(f_{t}p_{t})+\frac{g_{t}^{2}}{2}\Delta p_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dp_{t}}{dt}=-\mathrm{div}(f_{t}p_{t})+\frac{g_{t}^{2}}{2}\Delta p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> represents the Laplace operator (in <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>), namely <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{div}\nabla" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>div</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{div}\nabla</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∇</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla</annotation></semantics></math> is the gradient operator (also in <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>). Rewriting this equation in the form of the continuity equation can be done as follows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Maoutsa et al., 2020a</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{dp_{t}}{dt}=-\mathrm{div}\Big(f_{t}p_{t}-\frac{g^{2}}{2}\frac{\nabla p_{t}}{p_{t}}p_{t}\Big)=-\mathrm{div}\Big(\big(f_{t}-\frac{g_{t}^{2}}{2}\nabla\log p_{t}\big)p_{t}\Big)=-\mathrm{div}\Big(w_{t}p_{t}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>div</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{dp_{t}}{dt}=-\mathrm{div}\Big(f_{t}p_{t}-\frac{g^{2}}{2}\frac{\nabla p_{t}}{p_{t}}p_{t}\Big)=-\mathrm{div}\Big(\big(f_{t}-\frac{g_{t}^{2}}{2}\nabla\log p_{t}\big)p_{t}\Big)=-\mathrm{div}\Big(w_{t}p_{t}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the vector field</p>
<table id="A4.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{t}=f_{t}-\frac{g_{t}^{2}}{2}\nabla\log p_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}=f_{t}-\frac{g_{t}^{2}}{2}\nabla\log p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">satisfies the continuity equation with the probability path <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore generates <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variance Exploding (VE) path</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The SDE for the VE path is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dy=\sqrt{\frac{d}{dt}\sigma_{t}^{2}}dw," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dy=\sqrt{\frac{d}{dt}\sigma_{t}^{2}}dw,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and increasing to infinity as <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\rightarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\rightarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The SDE is moving from data, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, at <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to noise, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, at <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> with the probability path</p>
<table id="A4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(y|y_{0})={\mathcal{N}}(y|y_{0},\sigma^{2}_{t}I)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(y|y_{0})={\mathcal{N}}(y|y_{0},\sigma^{2}_{t}I).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The conditional VF according to equation <a href="#A4.E40" title="In Conditional VFs for Fokker-Planck probability paths ‣ Appendix D Diffusion conditional vector fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a> is:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(y|y_{0})=\frac{\sigma_{t}^{\prime}}{\sigma_{t}}(y-y_{0})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(y|y_{0})=\frac{\sigma_{t}^{\prime}}{\sigma_{t}}(y-y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix D Diffusion conditional vector fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we get that the probability path</p>
<table id="A4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{t}(y|y_{0})={\mathcal{N}}(y|y_{0},\sigma_{1-t}^{2}I)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{t}(y|y_{0})={\mathcal{N}}(y|y_{0},\sigma_{1-t}^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">is generated by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{w}_{t}(y|y_{0})=-\frac{\sigma_{1-t}^{\prime}}{\sigma_{1-t}}(y-y_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{w}_{t}(y|y_{0})=-\frac{\sigma_{1-t}^{\prime}}{\sigma_{1-t}}(y-y_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which coincides with equation <a href="#S4.E17" title="In Example I: Diffusion conditional VFs. ‣ 4.1 Special instances of Gaussian conditional probability paths ‣ 4 Conditional Probability Paths and Vector Fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variance Preserving (VP) path</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The SDE for the VP path is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dy=-\frac{T^{\prime}(t)}{2}y+\sqrt{T^{\prime}(t)}dw," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dy=-\frac{T^{\prime}(t)}{2}y+\sqrt{T^{\prime}(t)}dw,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(t)=\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(t)=\int_{0}^{t}\beta(s)ds</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The SDE coefficients are therefore</p>
<table id="A4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{s}(y)=-\frac{T^{\prime}(s)}{2}y,\quad g_{s}=\sqrt{T^{\prime}(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{s}(y)=-\frac{T^{\prime}(s)}{2}y,\quad g_{s}=\sqrt{T^{\prime}(s)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{t}(y|y_{0})={\mathcal{N}}(y|e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(t)}y_{0},(1-e^{-T(t)})I)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{t}(y|y_{0})={\mathcal{N}}(y|e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(t)}y_{0},(1-e^{-T(t)})I).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Plugging these choices in equation <a href="#A4.E40" title="In Conditional VFs for Fokker-Planck probability paths ‣ Appendix D Diffusion conditional vector fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a> we get the conditional VF</p>
<table id="A4.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(y|y_{0})=\frac{T^{\prime}(t)}{2}\left(\frac{y-e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(t)}y_{0}}{1-e^{-T(t)}}-y\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(y|y_{0})=\frac{T^{\prime}(t)}{2}\left(\frac{y-e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(t)}y_{0}}{1-e^{-T(t)}}-y\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix D Diffusion conditional vector fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to reverse the time we get the conditional VF for the reverse probability path:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{w}_{t}(y|y_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{w}_{t}(y|y_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{T^{\prime}(1-t)}{2}\left(\frac{y-e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(1-t)}y_{0}}{1-e^{-T(1-t)}}-y\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{T^{\prime}(1-t)}{2}\left(\frac{y-e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(1-t)}y_{0}}{1-e^{-T(1-t)}}-y\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{T^{\prime}(1-t)}{2}\left[\frac{e^{-T(1-t)}y-e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(1-t)}y_{0}}{1-e^{-T(1-t)}}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{T^{\prime}(1-t)}{2}\left[\frac{e^{-T(1-t)}y-e^{-\frac{1}{2}T(1-t)}y_{0}}{1-e^{-T(1-t)}}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which coincides with equation <a href="#S4.E19" title="In Example I: Diffusion conditional VFs. ‣ 4.1 Special instances of Gaussian conditional probability paths ‣ 4 Conditional Probability Paths and Vector Fields ‣ Flow Matching for Generative Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F8.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2210.02747v2/figures/plots/2d_vf_reference.png" id="A4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/548;" width="548" height="548" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F8.fig6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="A4.F8.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2210.02747v2/2d_vf_flow_match_dif_0.svg" id="A4.F8.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/548;" width="548" height="548"></object>
